IELTS Listening Part 1 for an English-speaking learner: a phone or face-to-face conversation between two people in an everyday social context (booking, registering, enquiring), at the real length of about 4 to 5 minutes (600 words or more) even though only 5 of the part's 10 questions are asked, with form or note completion answered in no more than two words and/or a number. The answers are names (spelled out letter by letter), numbers, dates, prices or addresses said in the recording; one or two answers come right after a speaker corrects themselves. Accepted answers include the spelled name and numbers as digits, each within the two-word limit and listed once. Speakers mix the British and Australian accents listed.